Window the film canvas for a tiled film-edge export.
Co-created with DeepSeek, 2026-11-13. See NOTICE for project terms.

The film edge is a whole-canvas effect: the gate, the perforation pitch, the
edge print, the fog and the scan registration are all laid out once, from the
frame's size and the seeds. A phone cannot render the 69 MP canvas of a 135
edge in one storage buffer, so the canvas is rendered in windows of itself.

The layout stays the whole frame's on every tile -- the pitch comes from the
full frame, not from the window crop, and the off-frame cover is sampled with
the same millimetre coordinates. Only the dispatch rectangle and the source
rectangle move: a window of the canvas is filled from the corresponding crop
of the frame, plus the overlap the host discards.

`spk_overscan_layout_at` lays the canvas out without rendering, so a host can
learn the canvas size and the gate quads before it cuts the frame into tiles;
`spk_set_render_window` gives a session its window and its source rectangle.
Both default to the whole canvas and the whole frame, so the shipping
whole-frame path reads the same parameters and is byte for byte unchanged.
The date back is refused in a windowed render for now: its imprint is
rasterised in whole-canvas pixels and a glyph can straddle a window edge.

